// ===================== 7.3 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('7.3  The step the argument does not take'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **What you wrote and what they took, in two columns, and no explanation in between.** **Eight of ten have one**, and in six of the eight the reader\'s version is one step further and sounds like the same thing. **Read the six pairs out and ask the room to say what the step is in each** — **it is almost always from a count to a rate, or from a case to a policy.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Marks a step: **1** and **3**. ⚠ **Not 2, 4 or 5.** **2 is a hedge about the world** — _may well be safe_ — **and it does not name any step.** **4 is a formula that names nothing, which is 3.1\'s distinction arriving six units later.** ⚠ **5 is the one to spend time on**: _I am not an expert on loading_ **is about the writer and not about the inference**, and it tells a reader to go and find somebody who is.'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **it stops a reader taking a step the evidence does not support, by naming the step.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **His abstract said seven of eleven reached a diagnosis and the programme said _second samples improve diagnosis_** — **not wrong about his words and not what he had written.**   **2** **It is about the writer and not about the inference**, and it invites a reader to find somebody with standing and disregard the finding they were given.'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The hedging-does-not-close-it point is the one the class will resist and it should be demonstrated rather than argued.** **Write _seven of eleven reached a diagnosis_ on the board, then _seven of eleven cases possibly reached a diagnosis_, and ask the room for the conference-programme line for each.** **Both produce _second samples improve diagnosis_.** **The step is available in both, and a step that is available will be taken** — **which is why the repair is a named step and not a weaker claim.** ⚠ **Then the three forms, and the rule that each is used once**: _it does not follow that_ for the inference, _nothing in this establishes_ for the fact nobody has, _I make no claim about_ for the territory you have not entered.'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** _It does not follow that more second samples would raise the diagnosis rate._   **2** _Nothing in this establishes when the roller went out of service._   **3** _I make no claim about the welds, which I have not examined._   **4** ⚠ _The claim is larger than the count: the repair is to say "in the eleven cases where the two samples disagreed" and not to add a fourth refusal._   **5** ⚠ _Nine of the nineteen arrived after the rota ended at nine._ **No step is available and a refusal here would read as a writer apologising for a fact.**'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Item 4 is the governor on this cycle and without it the class will produce documents with six refusals in them.** **More than three in a paper and the reader concludes the writer does not believe the argument** — **and the right repair at that point is not a fourth refusal but a smaller claim.** **Say the number: three in a paper, one in an abstract**, and hold students to it in the marking.'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**1** **Step:** _so taking more second samples would help._ ⚠ _It does not follow that taking more second samples would raise the diagnosis rate._',
  '**2** ⚠ **No refusal needed.** _The box was signed for on 26 June and has not been seen since._ **An absence with a date.**',
  '**3** **Step:** _so the building is unsafe._ _It does not follow that the frame will fail; I have not calculated it on the installed sizes._',
  '**4** ⚠ **No refusal needed.** _Four of the twelve certificates are not in the file._',
  '**5** **Step:** _so the ten minutes caused the fall._ _Nothing in this establishes a cause: the ten minutes are the only candidate anybody has produced._',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('The step, and the sentence that names it. ⚠ **Rows 2 and 4 on both cards need no refusal**, each being a count or an absence with no inference attached. **Of the four that do, two take _it does not follow that_ and two take _nothing in this establishes_**, and the class should say which is which: **the first is for an inference a reader would draw and the second for a fact nobody has.** **A student who uses _it does not follow_ for a missing fact has written a refusal that refuses nothing.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**a** _**My finding:** eleven of a hundred and four October dispensings were against a superseded sheet._',
  '_**The step, in their words:** "so about one in nine of everything this branch dispenses is wrong."_ ⚠ _Which is a rate and I have a count, from one month._',
  '_**The sentence:** it does not follow that about one in nine of this branch\'s dispensing is against a superseded sheet; October is the only month examined and the other eleven are not known._',
  '**b** _(my partner, reading the finding without the refusal)_ _She concluded: "one in nine, every month."_ ⚠ _**With the refusal she said: "eleven in October."** Which is my finding, word for word._',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Dr Qabbani\'s abstract said that in seven of eleven cases a serological diagnosis was reached, and the conference programme said: second samples improve diagnosis. The programme was not wrong about his words and it was not what he had written. Mrs Tarabishi said that is what seven of eleven means, and it is not, and this is the step: seven of eleven is a count of what happened in eleven cases where the first sample failed, and improve diagnosis is a claim about what would happen if you took more second samples, which requires the ten who had none, and he has nothing about the ten. Mrs Khoury said hedging the claim would not have stopped it — seven of eleven cases possibly reached a diagnosis is a weaker sentence and the programme would have written the same line — and the repair is not a weaker claim but a named step. Mr Shihabi asked what a named step looks like, and it does not follow that taking more second samples would raise the diagnosis rate; the ten with no second sample are the group that would answer that and I have nothing about them. Twenty-eight words, and the programme could not have written its line. Mr Tayara asked whether that is not just saying what you do not know, and Mrs Oueidat said it is saying what the reader must not do, which is different: I do not know what the ten would show is a statement about the writer, and it does not follow that more second samples would help is a statement about the inference, and the inference is what the reader is about to make. Mrs Ajouz said so I am not an expert on loading is the wrong form, and it is the wrong form and worse than nothing, because it tells a reader the writer has no standing, which invites them to find somebody who has and to ignore the finding they were given: name the step, not yourself. Mr Zahreddine said he writes three of these in every opinion and had never thought of it that way, and gave the three: it does not follow that the frame will fail; nothing in this establishes when the roller went out of service; I make no claim about the welds, which I have not examined. Three sentences, about forty words, and the only part of the opinion nobody has ever argued with. Mrs Rizk asked whether a donor reads those, and a donor skips them and a lawyer reads nothing else, which is the arithmetic of it. Mr Attar asked how many is too many, and Dr Qabbani said three in a paper and one in an abstract: more than that and you have written an argument you do not believe, and the right repair then is not another refusal but a smaller claim.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The question the class should be asked after this report is about the programme and not about the abstract: was anybody careless?** **No.** **A programme line is nine words and the only nine words available from that abstract were the seven of eleven** — **and the writer had left the step open.** **Mr Zahreddine\'s arithmetic is the sentence to end on: a donor skips them and a lawyer reads nothing else, which is why forty words buy what they buy.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**✗** _I am not an expert on loading._ → **✓** that is about you.   **✗** Hedging the claim instead of naming the step. → **✓** the step is still available.   **✗** Four refusals in one document. → **✓** make the claim smaller.   **✗** _It does not follow_ for a missing fact. → **✓** _nothing in this establishes_.   **✗** A refusal with no remedy. → **✓** it reads as a disclaimer.'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **Three** — _it does not follow that_ **for the inference about more second samples**, _nothing in this series establishes_ **for why the ten were not taken**, and _I make no claim about_ **for cost.**   **2** **He makes no claim about cost**, ⚠ **because four minutes at two in the morning on a registrar with one pair of hands is a figure the series has not weighed and is not competent to weigh** — **and he gives the registrar\'s own count and attributes it to her.**   **3** **They cannot answer the question they were kept for**, ⚠ **because the note that asked for a second sample named no decider and produced no reasons.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
