out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Ajouz had a registration file returned in March with one sentence quoted and nothing else mentioned: the dispensary has operated without incident since 2019. The officer asked what an incident is, who decides, and where the record is. Mrs Tarabishi said all three are fair questions, and all three are fair and she could answer none of them from any document she holds — the sentence was true and it was not hers to make, because without incident is a finding by somebody with a definition and a register, and she has neither. Mr Zahreddine said the repair is not to hedge it, and the repair was to say what she actually has: the incident book has nine entries since 2019, of which six are cold-chain and three are labelling; it is kept by the branch pharmacist and she has copied it. Longer, specific, and nothing in it to take. Mr Shihabi asked for the difference between that and hedging, because the room will hear them as the same, and hedging makes a claim vaguer and sizing makes it smaller: the dispensary has operated largely without incident is hedged and still unanswerable, and nine entries, six and three is small and completely answerable, and a reader can check it, which is what takes the handle away. Dr Qabbani said so the page gets longer, and about a third longer, and the second version was accepted in eleven days where the first had been out for seven weeks. Mrs Khoury gave the arithmetic the class should hear: four of her six paragraphs were already fine, so a page with nothing to take is not a rewritten page but a page with two sentences repaired. Mr Tayara asked how you find the two, and Mrs Oueidat said 7.1, and it takes eleven minutes: the two sentences are always the ones with a word in them that somebody else would have to define — incident, satisfactory, appropriate, adequate, in good order. Mrs Rizk said her donors\' forms are made of those words, and their forms ask for them and their lawyers cannot use them: answer the form\'s word and then give the count underneath. Mrs Tarabishi asked about a page where every claim is already a count, and then there is nothing to do and the room should hear that too: four of her six paragraphs needed nothing at all, and she nearly rewrote them because the file had come back. And Mr Attar asked whether there is a page where nothing can be done, and Mrs Ajouz said a page where the claim is larger than anything you have counted — then the repair is not in the writing at all, and the only honest page is the smaller claim.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **Seven weeks against eleven days is the arithmetic to leave on the board.** **Then Mrs Khoury\'s correction, which is the thing that stops a class over-applying this: four of six paragraphs were already fine.** **And the last exchange is the one to end on** — **a page where the claim is larger than anything you have counted has no repair in the writing at all**, and a student who keeps rewriting such a page is doing the one thing this unit cannot help with.'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**✗** _Largely without incident._ → **✓** hedged and still unanswerable.   **✗** _Satisfactory_ with nothing under it. → **✓** answer the word, then count.   **✗** Rewriting six paragraphs. → **✓** two of them needed it.   **✗** A count with no keeper. → **✓** who holds the record?   **✗** Sizing a claim larger than the count. → **✓** nothing in the writing will do it.'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **Nine entries since January 2019, six cold-chain and three labelling, kept by the pharmacist on duty, all nine copied at Appendix C, paginated and with nothing removed**; **and 4.2 says what the nine do not cover** — **an incident nobody entered is not in the book and she has no way of knowing how many there have been.**   **2** **Whether the staffing is sufficient**, ⚠ **because that is a judgement about volume and hours that the file does not have the figures for.**   **3** **The first version said the dispensary had operated without incident since 2019**; ⚠ **the book is a record of what was entered and she does not define what an incident is.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
